    <sys:String x:Key="LeaseHelp.Title">DHCP lease duration — what it really changes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LeaseHelp.Heading">Why the lease duration matters</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LeaseHelp.Bullet1">The lease outlives the server shutdown: the device keeps its IP until expiry or manual release.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LeaseHelp.Bullet2">Short (5-10 min): the bench cleans itself up after each session.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LeaseHelp.Bullet3">Long (12-24 h): friendly for a long demo, but the device will keep its IP even with the app closed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LeaseHelp.Footer">The duration is sent to devices in DHCP option 51 (OFFER and ACK). Change it in the “Lease duration” list; click “Apply” if the server is already running.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LeaseHelp.Close">Close (Esc)</sys:String>

